# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings regardless of the checking-out
# machine's git config. This repo's core.autocrlf=true would otherwise
# rewrite these to CRLF on a Windows checkout, and a CRLF shebang line
# (`#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`) fails on Linux with "bad interpreter: ... no such
# file or directory" -- exactly the kind of Windows/Linux portability bug
# W15 exists to close. This matters in particular because these scripts are
# meant to be deployed by cloning this repo directly onto a Linux host.
*.sh text eol=lf
